      "name": "us-co-snap-fy2024",
      "notes": "Compile-time overlay that replays the Colorado SNAP benefit composition against fiscal year 2024 federal parameters. The rulespec-us monorepo ships the composition wired to the FY 2026 cost-of-living (COLA) parameter set, so this overlay rewrites the three USDA cola module ids (fy-2026-cola -> fy-2024-cola) across the composition and every module that imports them, then patches the four Colorado standard-utility-allowance amounts down to their FY 2024 values. The overlay is materialized as a single self-contained rulespec root (a real copy of the us and us-co prefix trees with the rewrites and patches applied) and compiled with that root alone: the engine unions module ids across repo roots rather than shadowing, so a sparse overlay fronting the monorepo would compile both cola vintages and abort with a duplicate-rule error. This is a stopgap: once TheAxiomFoundation/rulespec-us#759 lands the parameter-set inversion (a program selects its cola set by period rather than by hardcoded module id), the fiscal year becomes a run-time choice and this overlay retires. The copy-then-patch discipline follows the EUROMOD platform patcher precedent in axiom_oracles/adapters/euromod/_runner.py, which patches policy switches and DefConst values into a copy of the model tree because the source model must never be mutated in place.",
